standard article 5 1 is identified by "http://data.europa.eu/leg/lomo/test#Standard_Article5_1".

standard article 5 1 is a standard.

standard article 5 1 has the title "Article 5(1) Technical Standards".

standard article 5 1 has the description "ESMA, in close cooperation with the ESCB, may develop draft regulatory technical standards to further specify the conditions referred to in Article 5(1) for security settlement systems and clearing systems. EBA, in close cooperation with the ESCB, may develop draft regulatory technical standards to further specify the conditions referred to in Article 5(1) for payment systems.".


standard article 13 13 is identified by "http://data.europa.eu/leg/lomo/test#Standard_Article13_13".

standard article 13 13 is a standard.

standard article 13 13 has the title "Article 13(13) Implementing Technical Standards".

standard article 13 13 has the description "ESMA shall, in close cooperation with the ESCB, develop draft implementing technical standards to specify, for securities settlement systems and clearing systems: (a) the uniform electronic formats for the application for registration referred to in paragraph 1, to be submitted to the central database; (b) the uniform electronic formats for the application for designation referred to in Article 4(1), to be submitted to the central database.".


standard article 13 15 is identified by "http://data.europa.eu/leg/lomo/test#Standard_Article13_15".

standard article 13 15 is a standard.

standard article 13 15 has the title "Article 13(15) Regulatory Technical Standards".

standard article 13 15 has the description "EBA shall, in close cooperation with the ESCB, develop, for payment systems, draft regulatory technical standards to further specify the information to be provided in: (a) an application for registration as referred to in paragraph 1 with a view to demonstrate that the applicant third-country system operator and the third-country system comply with all relevant requirements set out in this Article, including the conditions set out in Article 14, and to specify the information the application shall contain on the members, of the third-country system, established in the Union; (b) an application for designation as referred to in Article 4(1), with a view to demonstrate that the applicant system operator and the system comply with all the relevant requirements of this Regulation.".


